# 🧞‍♂️ **R-GENIE SYSTEM-SPECIFIC STRUCTURE**

**ALL R-GENIE operations follow this SYSTEM-SPECIFIC STRUCTURE**

## 📁 **MANDATORY USER WORKSPACE LOCATIONS**

**✅ ALWAYS USE SYSTEM-SPECIFIC FOLDERS:**
```
project/
├── input_01_design/         # DESIGN SYSTEM INPUTS
├── output_01_design/        # DESIGN SYSTEM OUTPUTS
├── input_02_api/           # API SPECIFICATION INPUTS
├── output_02_api/          # API SPECIFICATION OUTPUTS
├── input_03_app/           # APP DEVELOPMENT INPUTS
├── output_03_app/          # APP DEVELOPMENT OUTPUTS
├── input_03_01_dataweave/  # DATAWEAVE INPUTS
├── output_03_01_dataweave/ # DATAWEAVE OUTPUTS
├── input_04_munit/         # MUNIT TESTING INPUTS
├── output_04_munit/        # MUNIT TESTING OUTPUTS
├── input_05_readme/        # DOCUMENTATION INPUTS
├── output_05_readme/       # DOCUMENTATION OUTPUTS
├── input_06_review/        # CODE REVIEW INPUTS
└── output_06_review/       # CODE REVIEW OUTPUTS
```

**❌ NEVER CREATE IN SUBSYSTEMS:**
- `r-genie/{subsystem}/input/` or `output/`
- `r-genie/{subsystem}/template/` or `example/`

**R-GENIE SUBSYSTEMS contain ONLY:**
- ✅ `rules/` - AI agent behavior rules
- ✅ `lib/` - Processing scripts (if applicable)
- ✅ `README.md` - System documentation

## 🚨 **ENFORCEMENT**

**✅ ALWAYS:** Use system-specific input_{system}/output_{system} folders, keep subsystems clean  
**❌ NEVER:** Create input/output in r-genie subsystems, mix user content with system files
